{"id": "36862", "revid": "162256", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=36862", "title": "Tuckahoe", "text": "Tuckahoe is a village in Westchester County, New York and a small suburb of New York City.\nGet around.\nTuckahoe's two train stations are, on Depot Square, and, in the northern portion of the village bordering the Crestwood area of both Tuckahoe and Yonkers. Both stations are served by Metro-North's Harlem Line. However, Westchester's bus system, the also serves Tuckahoe. However, owing to the small size of the village, you can pretty much walk anywhere.\nDo.\nThe trolley stops at places like: \nBut there's also..."}
